  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Nucleophilicity &nbsp;is directly proportional to the electro density on donor atom and the size of donor atom (in gas)</p><p>And Stronger the base, greater the nucleophilicity.</p><p>As weak acid will have a strong conjugate base&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>is stronger base than ammonia.Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;is a stronger nucleophile than ammonia</p>"
  }
